      "_comment": "Samples at preprocess_params.sample_freq (200Hz) -- the cut_event_window pad point, round(pre_event_seconds * sample_freq) = round(1.0*200) = 200 for every event-anchored dataset (BCICIV2a/BCICIV1_Train/Inria_Train, and BCICIV2b/Inria_Test/BCICIV1_Test which share the same loaders). EEGMMIdb stays 0/unshifted: it labels T0 (rest) as its own class with ~0 real pre-event headroom, so it's deliberately excluded from the pre/post-event buffer (see datas/EEGMMIdb/loader.py, docs/model-analysis-checklist.md). Mirrors config/analysis.json's check.event_onset_sample -- used by model/base_checker.py's _lookup_event_onset to draw the event line in training-time recon_signal/stamp_by_patch snapshots too, not just check_model.py's standalone analysis.",
